hermes v0.23.0: a user message sent while a foreground terminal command
runs moves the command to the background (still running, notify on
completion) on every busy path, not only for a text-only redirect.

Symptom: sometimes a message sent mid-command killed the command
("[Command interrupted]", exit 130) instead of yielding it.

Cause: only AIAgent.redirect() (text-only busy messages in interrupt
mode) asks the tool workers to yield. Every other busy path either hard-
or soft-interrupts, and the terminal wait loop kills on the interrupt
bit: the TUI/desktop prompt.submit fallback for older runtimes, a message
with attachments (queued, but the turn stays parked behind the command
until it exits), the messaging gateway's interrupt for media/voice
(gateway/run_inbound.py, run_busy.py, run_turn.py's pending-message
monitor) and the classic CLI's typed interrupt.

Fix: agent/interrupt_control.py yield_tool_commands(agent, wait) requests
the yield for every tool worker while tools execute and (with wait) blocks
up to 2 s until the terminal took it; each of those paths calls it first.
The attachment path only yields (the message stays queued as the next
turn, with its images). Explicit stops (/stop, Esc, Ctrl-C, the Stop
button, session.interrupt) still kill. Non-local terminal backends have no
host process to adopt and keep the old behaviour.

